WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.950
The rest of the shelf.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.350
Tide and current predictions come from NOAA’s Tides and Currents service.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:15.925
But the exam uses pages from the classic printed Tide Tables and Tidal Current Tables, so you need to know how those are laid out.

4
00:00:16.175 --> 00:00:18.950
We’ll practice them in the next two lessons.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.100
The Navigation Rules handbook, which you know well by now.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.675
Chart Number One, the key to every chart symbol.

7
00:00:26.925 --> 00:00:31.200
And the Code of Federal Regulations, the law you operate under.

8
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.525
Two titles matter to you.

9
00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:38.025
Title thirty-three is navigation and navigable waters.

10
00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:44.500
Title forty-six is shipping, which includes uninspected passenger vessels and your license.

11
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.025
Here’s how I keep them apart.

12
00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:50.500
Thirty-three is about the water.

13
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.100
Forty-six is about the boat and the people on it.
